# Line endings, settled once.
#
# core.autocrlf=true on this machine rewrote endings on every checkout, so every
# git command printed "LF will be replaced by CRLF" for files nobody had touched.
# The noise made real warnings easy to miss. Declaring it here makes the answer a
# property of the repo rather than of whoever cloned it.
#
# LF everywhere: Node reads it, the tests read it, and .gs files are pasted into a
# web editor that does not care. Nothing in this project needs CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only helpers, if any are ever added, keep CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary — never touch these.
*.png binary
*.docx binary
*.xlsx binary
*.zip binary
*.db binary
